1. Amazon EC2

EC2 = Elastic Compute Cloud

EC2 provides virtual servers (instances) in the AWS Cloud.

You can configure an instance according to your requirements, such as:

CPU
RAM
Storage
Operating System
Network configuration
AWS
 ↓
EC2
 ↓
Virtual Machine / Instance
 ↓
Application

2. Creating an EC2 Instance

Basic process:

Choose AMI
   ↓
Choose Instance Type
   ↓
Configure Instance
   ↓
Configure Storage
   ↓
Configure Security
   ↓
Launch Instance

After launching, the instance can be accessed remotely.

3. Connecting to Linux Instance

For a Linux EC2 instance, SSH can be used for remote access.

Basic commands practiced:

sudo -i
sudo apt update
nginx -t
sudo apt install nginx
systemctl status nginx

These commands help with administration and checking services on a Linux server.

4. Bootstrap / User Data Script

A bootstrap script can automatically execute commands when an EC2 instance starts.

Example:

#!/bin/bash

apt-get update
apt-get install nginx -y

echo "Welcome to AWS" > /var/www/html/index.html

This can automatically:

Update packages
Install software
Configure the server
Deploy basic application files
